### The full happy path, through the gateway, with real payloads.
#
# This file is the contract the client is built against. Every request goes to the gateway, which is
# the only thing with a published port; budget-core cannot be reached directly, by design.
#
# Conventions that hold everywhere below:
#
# - Money is a string with two decimals, "1570.00", in both directions. Numbers are accepted on input
#   too, but strings are what comes back, because a JSON number cannot promise two decimals.
# - Anything the client sends back as an identifier is a lowercase key: "groceries", "locked", "high",
#   "regular", "medium". Keys are for machines. Every key arrives beside a "label" written for a person,
#   and the label is what gets rendered - never the key, and never an upper-case constant.
# - Everything under /api/v1 belongs to the signed-in user, and to nobody else. There is no user id in
#   any URL or body: the gateway takes it from the token and budget-core scopes every query by it.
# - Errors are RFC 9457 problem details: {"type","title","status","detail","instance"}. "detail" is
#   written to be shown to the user as-is.
#
# Get a token by signing in through Supabase (the client does this with @supabase/supabase-js) and
# paste the access token below.

@gateway = http://localhost:8090
@token = paste-a-supabase-access-token-here

### 0. Without a token nothing gets past the gateway: 401, and budget-core never sees the request.
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/plan

### 1. Countries we hold figures for.
# -> [{"code":"LB","name":"Lebanon","note":"Prices in Lebanon are quoted in US dollars ..."}, ...]
GET {{gateway}}/api/catalogue/countries
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2. Cities in one country. "id" is the only lookup key there is; send it back exactly.
# -> [{"id":"beirut","name":"Beirut","region":"Beirut","basis":"Researched by us",
#      "explanation":"We gathered this from listings and local prices. ...","gathered":"2026-09-01"}]
GET {{gateway}}/api/catalogue/countries/LB/cities
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3. For "my city isn't listed": the manual form, already filled in from the country estimate.
# "category" is the key to send the answer back under (step 7).
# -> [{"category":"rent","question":"About how much do you spend on rent each month?",
#      "why":"We do not have figures for your city yet, ...",
#      "covers":["Rent - your rent or mortgage payment"],"suggested":"350.00",
#      "basis":"A rough middle figure for Lebanon, gathered ... It is a starting point ..."}, ...]
GET {{gateway}}/api/catalogue/countries/LB/manual-form
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. Every choice the client offers, with the words to offer it in. Each entry is
# {key, label, covers}: send the key back, render the label, show "covers" as the explanation.
# -> {"categories":[{"key":"groceries","label":"Groceries","covers":"food and household shopping ..."}],
#     "howWilling":[{"key":"locked","label":"Cannot be changed","covers":"We will never suggest ..."}],
#     "priorities":[{"key":"high","label":"Very important","covers":"Funded before anything you ..."}],
#     "lifestyles":[{"key":"regular","label":"Out regularly","covers":"Typical for someone who ..."}],
#     "mealBands":[{"key":"medium","label":"A normal meal out","covers":"a regular restaurant ..."}]}
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/choices
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4b. The two kinds of named commitment, worded for the category the user has just picked, so the
# label names their own category rather than leaving a hole for the client to fill in.
# -> [{"key":"already-counted","label":"Part of what I already spend on Subscriptions",
#      "covers":"we will not add it again - naming it just lets us tell you which thing to cut"},
#     {"key":"on-top","label":"Extra, on top of my Subscriptions",
#      "covers":"we will add it to what you spend, because nothing else has counted it yet"}]
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/choices/item-kinds?category=subscriptions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5. Where the user lives and how they live. Send "city" for a listed city, or "cityNotListed" with
# the name they typed (display only - it never selects a city) when theirs is not in the list.
# "lifestyle" and "leastForEnjoyingLife" may be null until asked; step 6 supplies the questions.
# -> 200 with the saved profile:
#    {"country":{"code":"LB","name":"Lebanon"},
#     "city":{"id":"beirut","name":"Beirut","basis":"Researched by us","explanation":"...","gathered":"2026-09-01"},
#     "cityNotListed":null,"lifestyle":{"key":"regular","label":"Out regularly"},
#     "incomeArrivesTaxed":true,"leastForEnjoyingLife":"250.00"}
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "country": "LB",
  "city": "beirut",
  "cityNotListed": null,
  "lifestyle": "regular",
  "incomeArrivesTaxed": true,
  "leastForEnjoyingLife": null
}

### 5b. Reading it back - the same shape, and 404 until they have told us where they live.
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. The questions still to ask, each explaining itself and pre-filled wherever we can.
# Money questions carry {question, why, covers, suggested, basis}; "key" says where the answer goes.
# -> [{"key":"least-for-enjoying-life","answerWith":"PUT /api/v1/profile leastForEnjoyingLife",
#      "question":"What is the least you would want to spend each month on enjoying life?",
#      "why":"We will never suggest cutting below this, even to reach a goal faster.",
#      "covers":["Going out and fun - nights out, ...","Eating out - ...","Clothes - ..."],
#      "suggested":"240.00","basis":"typical for someone in Beirut who goes out regularly ..."},
#     {"key":"spending:groceries","answerWith":"PUT /api/v1/spending groceries", ...}, ...]
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/questions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7. The user's own figure for a category - a manual-form answer, or a correction to ours.
# Applies to their plan immediately and to nobody else's, and beats every other source.
# -> {"category":{"key":"groceries","label":"Groceries"},"amount":"300.00","setOn":"2026-09-22",
#     "basis":{"label":"Your own figure","meaning":"You told us this, so we use it and nothing overrides it."}}
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/overrides/groceries
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": "300.00" }

###
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/overrides
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 8. The money the plan may work with, typed by the user (no bank connected).
# "balance" is taken whole: there is no share question on this path, because the user already chose
# what to type. Lowering it later takes money back out of the plan on the next run.
# "alreadySaving" is optional: what the user already moves into savings each month, shown beside the
# plan and never subtracted. Left out is not zero - left out lets a connected bank supply it from the
# last complete month, while "0.00" is the user saying they save nothing, which outranks the bank.
# -> {"monthlyIncome":"2000.00","balance":"20000.00","setAside":"0.00",
#     "explanation":"We plan with exactly what you told us you have. ...",
#     "alreadySaving":"150.00","alreadySavingExplanation":"What you already move into savings ..."}
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/money
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "monthlyIncome": "2000.00", "balance": "20000.00", "alreadySaving": "150.00" }

### 8b. What the plan is currently working with. 404 until step 8.
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/money
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9. What the user actually spends each month, by category key. Leave a category out and the plan
# fills it in, in this order: a connected bank's figure for the last complete month, which the line
# then names ("measuredFrom": "what you spent in February 2026"), and failing that the local figure,
# which the line flags ("assumed": true). What the user states here outranks both.
# -> {"rent":"500.00","groceries":"380.00","dining-out":"200.00","entertainment":"120.00"}
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/spending
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rent": "500.00",
  "groceries": "380.00",
  "subscriptions": "40.00",
  "dining-out": "200.00",
  "entertainment": "120.00"
}

### 9b. What they have told us so far, by category key. A category missing here is one the plan
# assumes at the local figure.
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/spending
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 10. A named commitment, so advice can name it. "kind" is "already-counted" (already inside that category's
# figure - naming it changes no total) or "on-top" (extra, nothing else has counted it).
# "howWilling" is the user's own answer; "locked" means the plan never suggests cutting it.
# -> {"id":"gym","label":"Gym membership","category":{"key":"subscriptions","label":"Subscriptions"},
#     "amount":"30.00","howWilling":{"key":"locked","label":"Cannot be changed"},
#     "kind":{"key":"already-counted","label":"Part of what I already spend on Subscriptions","meaning":"we will not add it again ..."}}
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/line-items/gym
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "label": "Gym membership",
  "category": "subscriptions",
  "amount": "30.00",
  "howWilling": "locked",
  "kind": "already-counted"
}

###
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/line-items
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 10b. Removing a named commitment. 204, and 404 if it is not one of theirs.
DELETE {{gateway}}/api/v1/line-items/gym
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 11. The first plan. Every recompute appends a snapshot; nothing ever edits an old one.
# -> 201, Location: /api/v1/plan/history/{id}, body is the plan (shape under step 13).
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/plan
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 12. Add a goal. There is no "already saved" field, on purpose: what a goal has already is worked
# out from the balance in step 8, so the same dollars can never be counted towards a goal twice.
# Adding a goal recomputes the whole plan and returns it.
# -> 201 {"goal":{"id":"...","name":"Car","target":"12000.00","deadline":"2027-06-30",
#                 "priority":{"key":"high","label":"Very important"},"finishFirst":false},
#         "plan":{ ...the new plan... },"waitingFor":null}
# "waitingFor" is a sentence instead, and "plan" is null, when the goal is saved but a plan cannot be
# made yet - before any income is known, for instance.
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/goals
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Car", "target": "12000.00", "deadline": "2027-06-30", "priority": "high" }

### 13. A competing, higher-priority goal. Watch the re-ranking in the returned plan.
#
# The plan, which is also what GET /api/v1/plan and GET /api/v1/plan/history/{id} return:
# {"id":"...","takenAt":"2026-09-22T10:15:30Z","asOf":"2026-09-22",
#  "reason":"You added a goal: Emergency fund",
#  "money":{"monthlyIncome":"2000.00","balanceInScope":"20000.00","setAside":"0.00",
#           "putTowardGoals":"20000.00","leftUnassigned":"0.00",
#           "runway":{"label":"Your money is not running down","months":null}},
#  "surplus":{"amount":"610.00",
#             "explanation":"What is left each month if spending comes down to the figures below. ...",
#             "assumedReduction":"70.00",
#             "assumedReductionExplanation":"The monthly figure above already assumes you make these changes. ...",
#             "reductions":[{"label":"Eating out, going out and clothes","from":"320.00","to":"250.00","by":"70.00"}],
#             "lines":[{"id":"groceries","label":"Groceries","category":{"key":"groceries","label":"Groceries"},
#                       "spent":"380.00","localFigure":"300.00","counted":"300.00","assumed":false,
#                       "basis":{"label":"Your own figure","explanation":"...","gathered":"2026-09-22","ageing":null}}],
#             "leastForEnjoyingLife":"250.00","alreadySaving":"150.00"},
#  "goals":[{"id":"...","name":"Emergency fund","priority":{"key":"critical","label":"Must happen"},
#            "target":"6000.00","fromBalance":"6000.00","stillNeeded":"0.00","deadline":"2027-03-31",
#            "monthlyNeeded":"0.00","monthlyFunded":"0.00","shortBy":"0.00","finishFirst":false,
#            "status":{"label":"Already covered","meaning":"..."}}, ...],
#  "cuts":{"suggested":[{"label":"Subscriptions","category":{"key":"subscriptions","label":"Subscriptions"},
#                        "by":"10.00","howWilling":{"key":"essential","label":"Very important"}}],
#          "suggestedTotal":"10.00","alreadyAssumed":"70.00","totalChange":"80.00",
#          "totalChangeExplanation":"Everything you would change to make this plan work. ...",
#          "stillShort":"0.00","options":[]},
#  "hints":[{"label":"Rent","hint":"a roommate, or renegotiating the lease at renewal, ..."}],
#  "leftOver":{"amount":"0.00","explanation":"..."}}
#
# "cuts.suggested" is never shown without "alreadyAssumed" and "totalChange" beside it: the monthly
# figure is not money in hand, and the suggested cuts are only the part on top of what it assumed.
# "hints" are sentences, never numbers - do not render them in a total.
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/goals
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Emergency fund", "target": "6000.00", "deadline": "2027-03-31", "priority": "critical" }

### 14. Let the car take the balance first, ahead of priority order. Returns the recomputed plan.
# Send {"goalId": null} to go back to priority order.
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/goals/finish-first
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "goalId": "paste-the-car-goal-id" }

### 15. Change a goal - for example, give it more time. Returns {"goal":..., "plan":...}.
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/goals/paste-the-car-goal-id
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Car", "target": "12000.00", "deadline": "2027-12-31", "priority": "high" }

###
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/goals
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 16. Take money back out of the plan. The next plan hands it back - a new snapshot, never an edit.
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/money
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "monthlyIncome": "2000.00", "balance": "5000.00" }

###
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/plan
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 17. The latest plan, without recomputing. 404 until the first plan exists.
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/plan
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 18. Every plan ever made, newest first, each saying why it was made and what it changed.
# -> [{"id":"...","takenAt":"...","reason":"You added a goal: Emergency fund",
#      "changes":{"goalsAdded":["Emergency fund"],"goalsRemoved":[],
#                 "surplus":{"before":"610.00","after":"610.00"},
#                 "goals":[{"id":"...","name":"Car",
#                           "before":{"status":"On track","monthlyFunded":"0.00","fromBalance":"12000.00"},
#                           "after":{"status":"Behind","monthlyFunded":"520.00","fromBalance":"0.00"}}]}}]
# The oldest entry has "changes": null - there was nothing before it.
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/plan/history
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 19. One past plan, exactly as it was.
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/plan/history/paste-a-snapshot-id
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 20. "Can I afford this today?" Pick a meal band from /choices, or price something yourself with
# "price" and "label". "spentThisMonth" is what has already gone on that category this month: send it
# and it is used, leave it out and a connected bank answers it from the user's own transactions. With
# neither, the request is refused rather than assuming nothing has been spent - which would make every
# answer look more affordable than it is. Where their own payments cover a band, "basis" on the price
# reads "What you actually pay" instead of "Our estimate".
# -> {"verdict":{"label":"This works if you ease off afterwards","meaning":"..."},
#     "category":{"key":"dining-out","label":"Eating out"},
#     "purchase":{"label":"A normal meal out","covers":"...","price":"10.00",
#                 "basis":{"label":"Our estimate","meaning":"..."}},
#     "allowance":"200.00","allowanceBasis":"...","spentThisMonth":"120.00","left":"80.00",
#     "daysLeft":9,"perDay":"8.88",
#     "catchUp":{"perDayAfter":"8.75","lessPerDay":"0.13","days":8,"fitsThisMonth":true,
#                "runsIntoNextMonth":"0.00"},
#     "cheaper":{"label":"Cheap and cheerful","covers":"...","price":"6.00","basis":{...},
#                "verdict":{"label":"You can afford this","meaning":"..."}}}
# "cheaper" is always shown beside a warning: a warning on its own is a scold.
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/decisions/afford
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "category": "dining-out", "band": "medium", "spentThisMonth": "120.00" }

###
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/decisions/afford
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "category": "clothing", "label": "Winter jacket", "price": "200.00", "spentThisMonth": "0.00" }

### 21. "Give me more for this, and take it from the rest." Raise a line by dollars ("amount") or by a
# whole percentage of the balance in scope ("percentOfBalance") - one or the other. Line ids are the
# category keys and the line-item ids from step 10. This is a proposal; nothing is saved.
# -> {"outcome":{"label":"Done - here is what gives","meaning":"..."},
#     "granted":"50.00","stillShort":"0.00",
#     "changes":[{"id":"dining-out","label":"Eating out","from":"200.00","to":"250.00","by":"50.00"},
#                {"id":"entertainment","label":"Going out and fun","from":"120.00","to":"70.00","by":"-50.00"}],
#     "hints":[{"id":"gym","label":"Gym membership","hint":"off-peak or annual-paid memberships ..."}],
#     "options":[]}
# When "stillShort" is above zero, "options" carries the two real ways out, each with the request that
# acts on it: {"label":"Use more of your savings this month","meaning":"...","answerWith":"PUT /api/v1/money"}
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/decisions/rebalance
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "raise": "dining-out", "amount": "50.00" }

### 22. Removing a goal also recomputes, and the history shows what freeing its money did.
DELETE {{gateway}}/api/v1/goals/paste-a-goal-id
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 23. The user's connected banks and what their accounts hold. Before anything is connected,
# "connected" is false and both lists are empty; "explanation" is the sentence to show beside the
# connect button.
# "offered" says whether this user may connect a bank at all, which depends on the country in their
# profile: Plaid reaches US banks and no Lebanese ones. When false, "notOffered" is the sentence to
# show instead - why, and what to do instead - and there is no connect button to offer.
# -> {"offered":true,"notOffered":null,"connected":true,
#     "connections":[{"id":7,"connectedAt":"2026-09-24T10:00:00Z","lastUpdated":"2026-09-24T10:01:12Z",
#                     "status":"Up to date"}],
#     "accounts":[{"name":"Plaid Checking ••0000","kind":"Bank account","balance":"110.00",
#                  "meaning":"In the account","available":"100.00"},
#                 {"name":"Plaid Credit Card ••3333","kind":"Credit card","balance":"410.00",
#                  "meaning":"Owed on the card","available":null}],
#     "explanation":"We can only read your transactions and balances. ..."}
# "lastUpdated" is null and "status" says it is still importing until the first import finishes.
# Every balance travels with its "meaning": on a card or a loan the figure is owed, not held.
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/bank
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 24. Open the bank's own connect window. Pass "linkToken" to Plaid Link in the browser; the user's
# bank login is typed there and never reaches this service.
# -> {"linkToken":"link-sandbox-..."}
# 503 with a readable "detail" when the bank cannot be reached or the service has no bank keys.
# 409 with the "notOffered" sentence as "detail" when the user's country has no banks we can reach
# (step 25 refuses the same way).
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/bank/link-token
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 25. Finish connecting with the public token Plaid Link hands back. 202: the connection is saved and
# the import runs in the background. Returns the same shape as step 23.
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/bank/connections
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "publicToken": "public-sandbox-paste-from-plaid-link" }

### 26. Ask every connected bank for anything new, without waiting for it. Banks are also refreshed on
# their own every few hours.
# -> {"banks":1}
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/bank/refresh
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 27. Disconnect a bank: its access is revoked at Plaid and everything imported through it is
# deleted. 204; 404 for a connection that is not this user's.
DELETE {{gateway}}/api/v1/bank/connections/paste-a-connection-id
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
